      "claim": "In mice, HI-236 brain tissue concentrations were comparable to plasma concentrations, indicating that it easily crosses the blood-brain barrier.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "Multiple transferred in-vivo records consistently demonstrate meaningful CNS access after systemic administration, including PET brain binding, a brain/plasma ratio of 0.92, and comparable brain/plasma concentrations. Disrupted-barrier atenolol data were discounted as not representative of normal BBB function.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "Atenolol records C06 and C12 relied on osmotic BBB disruption and are not informative for normal CNS access.",
    "Some transferred records are qualitative or lack unbound brain concentrations, but direct brain/plasma and PET outcomes still support meaningful access."
  ],
